# Database (`packages/db`)

Local file libSQL only. Stay on `drizzle-orm` 0.45. Do not add Postgres,
Prisma, Turso Cloud, `better-sqlite3`, or `pg`.

```text
Hono → drizzle-orm/libsql → @libsql/client → file:…/agentic-kanban.db
```

- Open lazily (`getDb()` / proxied `db`) so Docker volumes exist before the
  first query. Do not connect at import time.
- Host default: `file:<repo>/data/agentic-kanban.db`. Compose:
  `DATABASE_URL=file:/data/agentic-kanban.db` bind-mounted from `./data`.
- `pingDatabase()` is `SELECT 1` and retries once after a stale handle.
- Schema folder: Better Auth tables in `schema/auth.ts` (`authSchema` for the
  `drizzleAdapter`). Tenant tables in `schema/workspace.ts` (`workspace`,
  `workspace_member`), `schema/project.ts` (`project`), `schema/column.ts`
  (`column`), `schema/task.ts` (`task`), `schema/comment.ts` (`comment`),
  and `schema/notification.ts` (`notification`). No `role`, slug, or owner.
  Comment HTTP and mention inserts yes. Notification helpers:
  `listNotificationsForUser` (inbox join + membership),
  `markNotificationReadForUser`.
- Reads: `listWorkspacesForUser`, `getProjectForMember` in `src/queries.ts`
  (membership + the row's `workspace_id`). Insert helpers are for tests.
  Seed upserts: `upsertWorkspace`, `upsertProject`, `upsertWorkspaceMember`,
  `upsertColumn`, `upsertTask`, plus `findUserIdByEmail` (select only).
  Board helpers: `getBoardForMember`, `moveTaskForMember`, task
  create/update/delete. Comment helpers: `listCommentsForMember`,
  `createCommentForMember` (via `getTaskForMember`; copy `workspace_id` /
  `project_id` from the task; resolve `mentionNames` to workspace
  members and insert `notification` kind `mention` in the same
  transaction). Inbox: `listNotificationsForUser`,
  `markNotificationReadForUser`. Never mass DELETE.
- Migrations: `bun run db:generate` then `bun run db:migrate` (once). After
  deleting `data/*.db*`, run `db:migrate` again. Never auto-run migrations.
  Never point the Mac API and Compose at the same `.db`.
- Every tenant-owned query must include an authorized `workspace_id`.
